# Keep the app out of search results.
#
# app.iqrra.com is a signed-in tool, not an audience page. It has nothing to
# rank for, and it cannot rank well anyway: every route serves the same empty
# Expo shell — same <title>, no description, no content until the bundle boots.
#
# It was worse than useless before this file. The SPA catch-all in _redirects
# answers 200 to EVERY path, existing or not, so /anything-at-all returned a
# page instead of a 404 — an unbounded set of identical thin URLs, all of them
# crawlable, all reachable from the three followed links on iqrra.com. Google's
# quality assessment is site-wide, so that sprawl is a drag on the one page
# that is actually trying to rank.
#
# A header, not robots.txt, and the difference matters: Disallow stops the
# crawl, and a crawler that never fetches the page never reads the noindex —
# so disallowed URLs linked from elsewhere stay in the index, listed with no
# title. To REMOVE pages you must let Googlebot in and hand it this header.
# public/robots.txt therefore allows everything on purpose.
#
# Cloudflare Pages reads _headers from the root of what it serves;
# `expo export --platform web` copies public/ verbatim into dist/, which is
# why this sits beside _redirects rather than in some build config.
/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow
